  "memo": "&lt;em&gt;Juniperus chinensis&lt;/em&gt;, commonly known as Chinese juniper, is an evergreen conifer native to Asia. This species can be grown as a shrub or small tree and can be pruned into a variety of shapes. It performs best in full sun, tolerates moderate drought, and grows well in rocky soil. The foliage is fragrant, and the species is dioecious, with female trees producing striking blue, berry-like cones.",
